<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Attleboro,_Massachusetts> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Attleboro** is a city in [Bristol County, Massachusetts](:Bristol_County%2C_Massachusetts), United States. It was once known as \"The Jewelry Capital of the World\" for its many [jewelry](:Jewelry) manufacturers. According to the [2020 census](:2020_United_States_Census), Attleboro had a population of 46,461.Attleboro is located about 10 miles (16 km) west of [Taunton](:Taunton%2C_Massachusetts), 10 miles north of [Providence](:Providence%2C_Rhode_Island), 18 miles (29 km) northwest of [Fall River](:Fall_River%2C_Massachusetts), and 39 miles (63 km) south of [Boston](:Boston)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
