<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Sweet_Honey_in_the_Rock> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Sweet Honey in the Rock is an all-woman, African-American a cappella ensemble. They are an American three-time Grammy Award–nominated troupe who express their history as black women through song, dance, and sign language. Originally a four-person ensemble, the group has expanded to five-part harmonies, with a sixth member acting as a sign-language interpreter. Although the members have changed over four decades, the group continues to sing and perform worldwide."@en .
