<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Robert_Vincent_(musician)> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Robert Vincent** (born 1981) born in [Crosby](:Crosby%2C_Merseyside), England, is a blues and [country music](:Country_music) singer-songwriter.Vincent is prominent in the 'Americana' genre, with apparent influences from both country and blues singers. Vincent tours extensively, mainly in a support capacity as of 2015. Vincent's first album was released in download and two forms of physical CD.Described by Andrew Harrison (editor of *[Q](:Q_%28magazine%29)*) as \"the scouse Springsteen\", Vincent is influenced by a range of music genres including Americana, 1970s English music and country music as well as his [Merseyside](:Merseyside) roots. He toured extensively throughout 2012 as well as releasing a string of singles and EPs.His debut album *Life In Easy Steps* was released by DB industries on 28 January 2013. His follow up, *I'll Make The Most Of My Sins* was released in February 2017.In 2020, the [Ethan Johns](:Ethan_Johns) produced album *In This Town You're Owned* was released. It went on to win the UK Americana Awards 'UK Album of the Year' and Vincent was named 'UK Artist of the Year'."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
