<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Snooky_Pryor> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**James Edward \"Snooky\" Pryor** (September 15, 1919 or 1921 – October 18, 2006) was an American [Chicago blues](:Chicago_blues) [harmonica](:Harmonica) player. He claimed to have pioneered the now-common method of playing amplified harmonica by cupping a small microphone in his hands along with the harmonica, although on his earliest records, in the late 1940s, he did not use this method."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
