<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Raekwon> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Corey Woods** (born January 12, 1970), better known by his [stage name](:Stage_name) **Raekwon The Chef**, or simply **Raekwon** (), is an American [rapper](:Rapping). He rose to prominence as a founding member of the hip-hop group [Wu-Tang Clan](:Wu-Tang_Clan), which achieved mainstream success following the release of their debut album, *[Enter the Wu-Tang (36 Chambers)](:Enter_the_Wu-Tang_%2836_Chambers%29)*, in 1993. Raekwon would subsequently pursue a solo career, releasing his first solo album, entitled *[Only Built 4 Cuban Linx...](:Only_Built_4_Cuban_Linx%2E%2E%2E)*, in 1995. The album received critical acclaim, and is regarded by many critics as one of the greatest hip-hop albums of all time, as well as a staple of 1990s rap.Whereas his next two albums, *[Immobilarity](:Immobilarity)* in 1999 and then *[The Lex Diamond Story](:The_Lex_Diamond_Story)* in 2003, drew mixed reviews, his fourth album, long delayed, *[Only Built 4 Cuban Linx... Pt. II](:Only_Built_4_Cuban_Linx%2E%2E%2E_Pt%2E_II)*, released in September 2009, was likened to *[The Godfather 2](:The_Godfather_Part_II)*. Recognized for his \"street epics\" that are \"straightforward yet linguistically rich,\" Raewkon is ranked among leading rappers. Meanwhile, he founded the record label ICE H20 Records."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
