<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Dolby_Pro_Logic> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Dolby Pro Logic is a surround sound processing technology developed by Dolby Laboratories, designed to decode soundtracks encoded with Dolby Surround. Dolby Stereo (also known as Dolby MP or Dolby SVA) was developed by Dolby in 1976 for analog cinema sound systems. The format was adapted for home use in 1982 as Dolby Surround when HiFi capable consumer VCRs were introduced. It was further improved with the Dolby Pro Logic decoding system after 1987."@en .
