<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Melissa_Etheridge> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Melissa Lou Etheridge (born May 29, 1961) is an American singer, songwriter, and guitarist. Her debut album, Melissa Etheridge, was released in 1988 and became an underground success. The album peaked at No. 22 on the Billboard 200 and its lead single, \"Bring Me Some Water\", garnered Etheridge her first Grammy Award nomination for Best Rock Vocal Performance, Female the following year. In 1993, Etheridge won her first Grammy Award for her single \"Ain't It Heavy\" from her third album Never Enough (1992). Later that year, she released what would become her mainstream breakthrough album: Yes I Am. Its tracks \"I'm the Only One\", \"Come to My Window\", and \"If I Wanted To\" all reached the Top 40 in the United States, while \"Come to My Window\" earned Etheridge her second Grammy Award in 1995. Yes "@en .
