<http://dbpedia.org/resource/St_Mary's_Church,_Nottingham> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The **Church of St Mary the Virgin** is the oldest [parish church](:Parish_church) of [Nottingham](:Nottingham), in [Nottinghamshire](:Nottinghamshire), England. It is the largest church after the [Cathedral](:Nottingham_Cathedral) in the city of Nottingham. The church was [Grade I listed](:Grade_I_listed) by the [Department for Digital, Culture, Media and Sport](:Department_for_Digital%2C_Culture%2C_Media_and_Sport) as a building of outstanding architectural or historic interest. It is one of only five Grade I listed buildings in the City of Nottingham.It is situated on [High Pavement](:High_Pavement) at the heart of the historic [Lace Market](:Lace_Market) district and is also known as St Mary's in the Lace Market. It is a member of the [Major Churches Network](:Major_Churches_Network), and part of the parish of All Saints', St Mary's and St Peter's, Nottingham."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
