<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Kermanshah> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Kermanshah** (Template:Lang-fa Template:IPA-fa, also known as **Kermashan** (Template:Lang-ku; romanized: Kirmaşan), is the capital of [Kermanshah Province](:Kermanshah_Province), located 525 kilometres (326 miles) from [Tehran](:Tehran) in the western part of [Iran](:Iran). According to the 2016 census, its population is 946,681 (2021 estimate 1,047,000). A majority of the people of Kermanshah are bilingual in [Southern Kurdish](:Southern_Kurdish) and [Persian](:Persian_language), and the city is the largest Kurdish-speaking city in Iran. Kermanshah has a moderate and mountainous climate. Most of the inhabitants of Kermanshah are [Shia](:Shia) Muslims, but there are also [Sunni](:Sunni) Muslims, [Christians](:Christianity_in_Iran), and followers of [Yarsanism](:Yarsanism)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
