<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Dizzee_Rascal> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Dylan Kwabena Mills** [MBE](:Order_of_the_British_Empire) (born 18 September 1984), better known by his stage name **Dizzee Rascal**, is a British [MC](:Rapping%23Emcees) and rapper. A pioneer of [grime music](:Grime_%28music_genre%29), his work has also incorporated elements of [UK garage](:UK_garage), [bassline](:Bassline_%28music_genre%29), [British hip hop](:British_hip_hop), and [R&B](:Contemporary_R%26B).Dizzee Rascal released his debut album *[Boy in da Corner](:Boy_in_da_Corner)* in 2003. It earned him the 2003 [Mercury Prize](:Mercury_Prize), and has since been considered a grime classic. Follow-up albums *[Showtime](:Showtime_%28Dizzee_Rascal_album%29)*, *[Maths + English](:Maths_%2B_English)*, and *[Tongue n' Cheek](:Tongue_n%27_Cheek)* were critically praised and certified platinum, with *Tongue n' Cheek* going platinum for sales exceeding 300,000 units in the United Kingdom. He has achieved 5 UK number-one singles, \"[Dance wiv Me](:Dance_wiv_Me)\", \"[Bonkers](:Bonkers_%28song%29)\", \"[Holiday](:Holiday_%28Dizzee_Rascal_song%29)\", \"[Dirtee Disco](:Dirtee_Disco)\" and \"[Shout](:Shout_%28Shout_for_England_song%29)\"."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
