<http://dbpedia.org/resource/George_Probert> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**George Arthur Probert, Jr.** (March 5, 1927 – January 10, 2015) was an American [jazz](:Jazz) clarinetist, [soprano saxophonist](:Soprano_saxophone), and bandleader active principally on the [Dixieland jazz](:Dixieland_jazz) revival circuit. He was born in Los Angeles.Probert was an [autodidact](:Autodidact) on his instruments. He played with [Bob Scobey](:Bob_Scobey) (1950–53) and then with [Kid Ory](:Kid_Ory)'s Creole Jazz Band. Between 1954 and 1969, he played in the [Firehouse Five Plus Two](:Firehouse_Five_Plus_Two) Dixieland revival band, an ensemble formed by animators from [Walt Disney](:Walt_Disney) Studios, and recorded with Disney composer [George Bruns](:George_Bruns) in 1957 and again in 1968. Probert led his own bands from 1973, touring America and Europe, especially [The Netherlands](:The_Netherlands). In 1997 Probert toured in England, Germany & the Netherlands with Big Bill Bissonnette's International Jazz Band; an all-star group which also featured Anthony \"Tuba Fats\" Lacen of New Orleans & British pianist Pat Hawes. He also worked as a television and movie music editor. He died on January 10, 2015, in Monrovia, California."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
