<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Cochabamba> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Cochabamba (Aymara: Quchapampa; Quechua: Quchapampa) is a city and municipality in central Bolivia in a valley in the Andes mountain range. It is the capital of the Cochabamba Department and the fourth largest city in Bolivia, with a population of 630,587 according to the 2012 Bolivian census. Its name is from a compound of the Quechua words qucha \"lake\" and pampa, \"open plain.\" Residents of the city and the surrounding areas are commonly referred to as cochalas or, more formally, cochabambinos."@en .
