<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Japanese_people> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The Japanese people (Japanese: 日本人, Hepburn: Nihonjin) are an ethnic group native to the Japanese archipelago in East Asia. Japanese people constitute 97.9% of the population of the country of Japan. Worldwide, approximately 129 million people are of Japanese descent; of these, approximately 122.5 million are residents of Japan. People of Japanese ancestry who live outside Japan are referred to as Nikkeijin (日系人), the Japanese diaspora. Depending on the context, the term ethnic Japanese (日本民族, Nihon minzoku) may be limited or not to mainland Japanese people, specifically the Yamato (as opposed to Ryukyuan and Ainu people). Japanese people are one of the largest ethnic groups in the world. In recent decades, there has also been an increase in the number of multiracial people with both Japan"@en .
