<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Vaasa> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Vaasa** (Template:IPA-fi; Template:Lang-sv, Template:IPA-sv, Sweden Template:IPA-sv), in the years 1855–1917 as **Nikolainkaupunki** (Template:Lang-sv; literally meaning \"city of [Nicholas](:Nicholas_I_of_Russia%29), is a city on the west coast of [Finland](:Finland). It received its charter in 1606, during the reign of [Charles IX of Sweden](:Charles_IX_of_Sweden) and is named after the Royal [House of Vasa](:House_of_Vasa). Vaasa has a population of 70,374 (31 December 2024) (approximately 120,000 in the Vaasa sub-region), and is the regional capital of [Ostrobothnia](:Ostrobothnia_%28region%29) (Template:Lang-sv; Template:Lang-fi. Vaasa is also well-known as a major [university](:University) and [college](:College) city in Finland.The city is bilingual with 64.7% of the population speaking [Finnish](:Finnish_language) as their first language and 23.2% speaking [Swedish](:Finland-Swedish). The surrounding Ostrobothnian municipalities (such as [Korsholm](:Korsholm) and [Malax](:Malax%29) have a [clear Swedish-speaking majority](:List_of_municipalities_of_Finland_in_which_Finnish_is_not_the_sole_official_language), which is why the Swedish language maintains a strong position in the city, making it the most significant [cultural center](:Culture) for Swedish-Finns.Vaasa is also known for Tropiclandia Water Park, which is located in the [Vaskiluoto Island](:Vaskiluoto_Island) right next to a local [spa hotel](:Spa). In the immediate vicinity of Tropiclandia was the now deserted [Wasalandia Amusement Park](:Wasalandia_Amusement_Park), which ceased operations in 2015 due to a small number of visitors."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
