<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Trap_music> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Trap is a subgenre of hip hop music that originated in the Southern United States during the late 1980s. The genre gets its name from the Atlanta slang word \"trap\", a house used exclusively to sell drugs. Trap music uses synthesized drums and is characterized by complex hi-hat patterns, tuned kick drums with a long decay (originally from the Roland TR-808 drum machine), and lyrical content that often focuses on drug use and urban violence. It utilizes very few instruments and focuses almost exclusively on snare drums and double- or triple-timed hi-hats."@en .
