<http://dbpedia.org/resource/José_M._Bayro_Corrochano> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "José M. Bayro Corrochano (born 1960) is a plastic artist Bolivian and nationalised Mexican that produces oil paintings, sculptures and engraving.It is known by his monumental works La pareja del Trompo (The Spin-top Couple) and El Hombre Azul (The Blue Man ) His first known monumental work was made and planted in the city of Puebla, in Mexico. El Hombre Azull (2006), is a sculpture that represents a worker concentrated in his daily work, which is standing seeing the fruit of his labor beside a peculiar chair. The sculpture is covered in talavera painted in blue tones, on a bed of white stone."@en .
