<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Hindustani_classical_music> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Hindustani classical music is the classical music of northern regions of the Indian subcontinent. It may also be called North Indian classical music or, in Hindustani, shastriya sangeet (śāstriya saṅgīt). It is played in instruments like the violin, sitar and sarod. It is mostly played by on violin as it supports all types of notes. Its origins from the 12th century CE, when it diverged from Carnatic music, the classical tradition in South India. Hindustani classical music arose in the Ganga-Jamuni Tehzeeb, a period of great influence of Perso-Arabic arts in the subcontinent, especially the Northern parts. This music combines the Indian classical music tradition with Perso-Arab musical knowledge, resulting in a unique tradition of gharana system of music education."@en .
