<http://dbpedia.org/resource/M.O.P.> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "M.O.P. (short for Mash Out Posse) is an American hip hop duo. Composed of East Coast rappers Billy Danze and Lil' Fame the duo are known for their aggressive lyrical delivery style. Although they maintain a strong underground following, they are mainly known for the song \"Ante Up\", released on their Warriorz album in 2000, and with which they have had mainstream success. The group has frequently collaborated with DJ Premier. Fame sometimes produces under the moniker Fizzy Womack, and has produced a significant number of tracks on all M.O.P. releases since 1996's Firing Squad, as well as work for other artists including Kool G Rap, Teflon and Wu-Tang Clan."@en .
