<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Vaasa> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Vaasa (Finnish: [ˈʋɑːsɑ]; Swedish: Vasa, Finland Swedish: [ˈvɑːsɑ], Sweden Swedish: [ˈvɑ̂ːsa]), in the years 1855–1917 as Nikolainkaupunki (Swedish: Nikolaistad; literally meaning \"city of Nicholas), is a city on the west coast of Finland. It received its charter in 1606, during the reign of Charles IX of Sweden and is named after the Royal House of Vasa. Vaasa has a population of 67,631 (31 December 2021) (approximately 120,000 in the Vaasa sub-region), and is the regional capital of Ostrobothnia (Swedish: Österbotten; Finnish: Pohjanmaa). Vaasa is also well-known as a major university and college city in Finland."@en .
