<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Örebro> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Örebro** ( [*UR-ə-BROO*](:Help%3APronunciation_respelling_key), Template:IPA-sv is the [sixth-largest city](:List_of_urban_areas_in_Sweden_by_population) in [Sweden](:Sweden), the seat of [Örebro Municipality](:%C3%96rebro_Municipality), and capital of the [Örebro County](:%C3%96rebro_County). It is situated by the [Närke](:N%C3%A4rke) [Plain](:Plain), near the lake [Hjälmaren](:Hj%C3%A4lmaren), a few kilometers inland along the small river [Svartån](:Svart%C3%A5n%2C_N%C3%A4rke), and has a population of approximately 126,000 in the [city proper](:City_proper). It is one of the largest inland hubs of the country, and a major [logistic](:Logistics) and commercial operating site.Örebro is home to [Örebro University](:%C3%96rebro_University), a [major university hospital](:%C3%96rebro_University_Hospital), a [medieval castle](:%C3%96rebro_Castle), the [water park](:Water_park) [Gustavsvik](:Gustavsvik) as well as several large shopping malls and the Oset-Rynningeviken nature reserve at the lakefront.Örebro is served by [Örebro Airport](:%C3%96rebro_Airport) 10 km (6 mi) southwest of the city, and by [Örebro Central Station](:%C3%96rebro_Central_Station), serviced by the [Mälaren Line](:M%C3%A4laren_Line) and [Western Main Line](:Western_Main_Line)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
