<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Young_M.A> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Katorah Kasanova Marrero** (born April 3, 1992), better known by her stage name **Young M.A** ([acronym](:Acronym) for **Young Me. Always**), is an American rapper. She first gained widespread recognition with the release of the quadruple-platinum hit single \"[Ooouuu](:Ooouuu)\", breaking the top 20 of the [*Billboard* Hot 100](:Billboard_Hot_100), boasting over 300 million YouTube views on the music video.After the success of her debut single, Young M.A was nominated for [BET](:BET) and [MTV](:MTV) Artist of the Year and Female Hip-Hop Artist of the Year awards. She began appearing on magazine covers. She has been featured in global ad campaigns for [Google Pixel 2](:Google_Pixel_2), [Beats By Dre](:Beats_By_Dr_Dre) and [Pandora](:Pandora_Radio). She has appeared on a variety of television shows and performed alongside [Alicia Keys](:Alicia_Keys) on *[The Tonight Show Starring Jimmy Fallon](:The_Tonight_Show_Starring_Jimmy_Fallon)*.In 2018, Young M.A was featured on the  [*Forbes* 30 Under 30](:Forbes_30_Under_30), the same year she launched the KWEENZ Foundation with her mother."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
