<http://dbpedia.org/resource/James_Lavelle> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "James Lavelle (born 22 February 1974) is an English electronic musician, record label owner and curator. He founded the Mo'Wax record label in 1992, and has been the only constant member of UNKLE. He directed the 2014 edition of the Meltdown festival on London's South Bank, and curated the 2016 exhibition \"Daydreaming with Stanley Kubrick\" at Somerset House. He was the subject of 2018 documentary film The Man From Mo'Wax."@en .
