<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Gary_Stewart_(singer)> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Gary Ronnie Stewart** (May 28, 1944 – December 16, 2003) was an American musician and songwriter, known for his distinctive [vibrato](:Vibrato) voice and his [outlaw country](:Outlaw_country) sound influenced by [southern rock](:Southern_rock). At the height of his popularity in the mid-1970s, *[Time](:Time_%28magazine%29)* magazine described him as the \"king of [honkytonk](:Honky_tonk).\" He had a series of country chart hits from the mid- to late 1970s, the biggest of which was \"[She's Actin' Single (I'm Drinkin' Doubles)](:She%27s_Actin%27_Single_%28I%27m_Drinkin%27_Doubles%29)\", which topped the U.S. country singles chart in 1975.On December 16, 2003, Stewart died of a [self-inflicted gunshot wound](:Suicide_by_gun), one month after the death of his wife."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
