<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Grimsby> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Grimsby, also Great Grimsby, is a port town and the administrative centre of North East Lincolnshire, Lincolnshire, England, on the south bank of the Humber Estuary close to the North Sea. It was the home port for the world's largest fishing fleet by the mid-20th century, but fishing then fell sharply. The Cod Wars denied UK access to Icelandic fishing grounds and the European Union used its Common Fisheries Policy to parcel out fishing quotas to other European countries in waters within 200-nautical-mile (370 km) of the UK coast."@en .
