<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Rob_Beckley> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Robert Benjamin \"Rob\" Beckley** (born August 20, 1975) is the [lead singer](:Lead_singer) and [rhythm guitarist](:Rhythm_guitar) of the [Christian rock](:Christian_rock) band [Pillar](:Pillar_%28band%29), which was voted Best Hard Rock Band in *[CCM Magazine](:CCM_Magazine)*'s 2006 Reader's Choice Awards. Beckley started the band in 1998 in Kansas.Beckley is married to Linda Beckley. In addition to being the band's frontman, he is also a soldier in the [United States Army Reserves](:United_States_Army_Reserves).Rob Beckley has contributed guest vocals to the songs such as, \"Numb\" by [Tait](:Tait_%28band%29), \"Rock On\" and \"Help me Change\" by [KJ-52](:KJ-52), \"Silent Screams\" by [Éowyn](:%C3%89owyn_%28band%29), and \"Indestructible\" by [Hardie Avenue](:Hardie_Avenue_%28band%29). Rob is currently working on a solo album that will be exclusively sold on Idefimusic."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
