<http://dbpedia.org/resource/English_folk_music> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The folk music of England is a tradition-based music which has existed since the later medieval period. It is often contrasted with courtly, classical and later commercial music. Folk music traditionally was preserved and passed on orally within communities, but print and subsequently audio recordings have since become the primary means of transmission. The term is used to refer both to English traditional music and music composed or delivered in a traditional style."@en .
