<http://dbpedia.org/resource/EMI> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "EMI Group Limited (originally an initialism for Electric and Musical Industries, also referred to as EMI Records Ltd. or simply EMI) was a British transnational conglomerate founded in March 1931 in London. At the time of its break-up in 2012, it was the fourth largest business group and record label conglomerate in the music industry, and was one of the \"Big Four\" record companies (now the \"Big Three\"). Its labels included EMI Records, Parlophone, Virgin Records, and Capitol Records, which are now owned by other companies."@en .
