<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Mo'_Wax> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Mo' Wax was a British record label founded by James Lavelle in 1992. The label was not co-founded by Tim Goldsworthy, as is often reported. Steve Finan became co-owner shortly after. Mo' Wax came to recognition for being at the forefront of trip hop, turntablism and alternative hip hop during the mid-1990s. The label is also responsible for bringing attention to the graffiti artist Futura 2000 by using his artwork on many of its releases in the early to mid-1990s. The label shut in 2002 and was celebrated in 2014 with an exhibition titled \"Urban Archaeology: 21 years of Mo' Wax\"."@en .
